<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="74256" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/DANC/270/74256.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2025" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025.xml">2025</calendarYear><term id="120251" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring.xml">Spring 2025</term><subject id="DANC" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/DANC.xml">Dance</subject><course id="270" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/DANC/270.xml">Dancing in Community I &amp; II</course></parents><sectionNumber>A  </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Dancing in Community II</sectionTitle><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Dancing in Community II is a mixed level course which allows dance majors to dance together once a week and ACTIVATE the various perspectives and skills of a multi-level community. Students enrolled in DANC 160 and 260 should also enroll in DANC 270. This course is an exploration of varied movement practices that build community and ensemble approaches to dancing. To provide a balance of training from a range of cultural origins and traditions, this course will DELVE into 2-3 contemporary movement approaches per semester.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2025-01-21Z</startDate><endDate>2025-05-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LAB">Laboratory</type><start>09:00 AM</start><end>10:30 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>F      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>2500</roomNumber><buildingName>Krannert Center for Perf Arts</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Gonzalez" firstName="G">Gonzalez, G</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>